{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-220299",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To solve compound \"and\" inequalities, we solve each inequality separately and then find their intersection.\n\n- First, we solve $-1\\le 2-x\\le 3\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le 2-x\\le 3 \\\\ -1-2 & \\le 2-x-2\\le 3-2 \\\\ -3 & \\le -x\\le 1 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-3) & \\ge (-1)\\cdot (-x)\\ge (-1)\\cdot 1 \\\\ 3 & \\ge x\\ge -1 \\\\ -1 & \\le x\\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14194110/assets/8fe1b22970eac80550ae9cc8d2da4b34df6a853c717a7dd402b164dfd99356ce.png)\n\n- Then, we solve $2x+1\\ge 5\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+1 & \\ge 5 \\\\ 2x+1-1 & \\ge 5-1 \\\\ 2x & \\ge 4 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{2} & \\ge \\frac{4}{2} \\\\ x & \\ge 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14194110/assets/ebcff9656b5f2a1fd80624639cb91baa0a28b696aa261b555cf449f1c62894d1.png)\n\nTo find the values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14194110/assets/7731bef503cf45a465945f81e0e2512f65c3e109a38d6d06afe74e17269f8c36.png)\n\nThus, the final solution is $2\\le x\\le 3.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
